IMPORT prelude

-- Legislation Act 2019 (New Zealand) -- LAYER 1: PART 2, REVISION ACTS AND INCORPORATION BY REFERENCE (ss 59 to 66).
-- Each rule is a provision of Part 2, so section 9(1) (nz-part2-principles.l4) says first whether it applies to the legislation in question.

§ `Section 59 -- Meaning of revision Act and old law`

-- src:410 | revision Act means a revision Bill prepared and certified under subpart 3 of Part 3, once that Bill has been enacted.
-- "revision Act means a revision Bill prepared and certified under subpart 3 of Part 3, once that Bill has been enacted."
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 59, definition of revision Act (src:410)
GIVEN `it was a revision Bill prepared and certified under subpart 3 of Part 3` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that Bill has been enacted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is a revision Act` `it was a revision Bill prepared and certified under subpart 3 of Part 3` `that Bill has been enacted` MEANS
    `it was a revision Bill prepared and certified under subpart 3 of Part 3` AND `that Bill has been enacted`

-- "old law, in relation to a revision Act, means the law as expressed in the Acts or parts of Acts repealed by and incorporated in the revision Act."
-- src:409 | old law, in relation to a revision Act, means the law as expressed in the Acts or parts of Acts repealed by and incorporated in the revision Act
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 59, definition of old law (src:409)
GIVEN `the Act or part is repealed by the revision Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Act or part is incorporated in the revision Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is old law in relation to the revision Act` `the Act or part is repealed by the revision Act` `the Act or part is incorporated in the revision Act` MEANS
    `the Act or part is repealed by the revision Act` AND `the Act or part is incorporated in the revision Act`

§ `Section 60 -- Revision Act is generally to have same effect as old law`

-- src:411 | 60 Revision Act is generally to have same effect as old law
-- src:412 | A revision Act’s provisions—
-- src:413 | are the provisions of the old law in rewritten form; and
-- src:414 | are intended to have the same effect as the corresponding provisions of the old law.
-- src:415 | This section is subject to section 62.
-- A revision Act's provisions are the provisions of the old law in rewritten form, and are intended to have the same effect as the corresponding provisions of the old law. This section is subject to section 62.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 60 (src:411) (src:412-415)
GIVEN `section 62 overrides section 60 for the provision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a provision of a revision Act is intended to have the same effect as the corresponding old law provision` `section 62 overrides section 60 for the provision` MEANS
    NOT `section 62 overrides section 60 for the provision`

§ `Section 61 -- Using old law as interpretation guide for revision Act`

-- src:416 | 61 Using old law as interpretation guide for revision Act
-- src:417 | If the meaning of a provision of a revision Act is unclear or gives rise to absurdity, the wording of the old law that corresponds to the provision must be used to ascertain the meaning of the provision.
-- If the meaning of a provision of a revision Act is unclear or gives rise to absurdity, the wording of the old law that corresponds to the provision must be used to ascertain the meaning.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 61 (src:416) (src:417)
GIVEN `the meaning of the provision is unclear` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision gives rise to absurdity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the wording of the corresponding old law must be used to ascertain the meaning` `the meaning of the provision is unclear` `the provision gives rise to absurdity` MEANS
    `the meaning of the provision is unclear` OR `the provision gives rise to absurdity`

§ `Section 62 -- Exceptions: when revision Act changes effect of old law`

-- src:418 | 62 Exceptions: when revision Act changes effect of old law
-- src:419 | Section 60 is overridden to the extent that a provision of a revision Act—
-- src:420 | is expressly provided by the revision Act to be intended to change the effect of the old law; or
-- src:421 | has a meaning that is expressly or by necessary implication to a different effect than the corresponding old law provision; or
-- src:422 | is enacted, amended, or repealed by legislation that is not a revision Act (for example, an amendment Act intended to change the effect of the old law).
-- Section 60 is overridden to the extent that a provision of a revision Act (a) is expressly provided by the revision Act to be intended to change the effect of the old law; or (b) has a meaning that is expressly
-- or by necessary implication to a different effect than the corresponding old law provision; or (c) is enacted, amended, or repealed by legislation that is not a revision Act.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 62 (src:418) (src:419-422)
GIVEN `the revision Act expressly provides that it is intended to change the effect of the old law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `its meaning is, expressly or by necessary implication, to a different effect than the corresponding old law provision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is enacted, amended or repealed by legislation that is not a revision Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 60 is overridden for the provision of a revision Act` `the revision Act expressly provides that it is intended to change the effect of the old law` `its meaning is, expressly or by necessary implication, to a different effect than the corresponding old law provision` `it is enacted, amended or repealed by legislation that is not a revision Act` MEANS
    `the revision Act expressly provides that it is intended to change the effect of the old law`
    OR `its meaning is, expressly or by necessary implication, to a different effect than the corresponding old law provision`
    OR `it is enacted, amended or repealed by legislation that is not a revision Act`

§ `Section 63 -- Interpretation (incorporation by reference)`

-- src:426 | material—
-- src:427 | means material referred to in section 64(1); but
-- src:428 | does not include anything incorporated by reference by that material
-- "material means material referred to in section 64(1); but does not include anything incorporated by reference by that material."
-- src:424 | 63 Interpretation
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 63, definition of material (src:424) (src:426-428)
GIVEN `it is referred to in section 64(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is incorporated by reference by other material` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is material for sections 64 to 66 and Schedule 2` `it is referred to in section 64(1)` `it is incorporated by reference by other material` MEANS
    `it is referred to in section 64(1)` AND (NOT `it is incorporated by reference by other material`)

-- "written material means material that represents or reproduces words, figures, or symbols (a) in a visible and tangible form by any means and in any medium; or (b) in a visible form in any medium by electronic means that
-- enables them to be stored in permanent form and be retrieved and read."
-- src:429 | written material means material that represents or reproduces words, figures, or symbols—
-- src:431 | in a visible form in any medium by electronic means that enables them to be stored in permanent form and be retrieved and read.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 63, definition of written material (src:429-431)
GIVEN `it represents or reproduces words, figures or symbols` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is in a visible and tangible form by any means and in any medium` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is in a visible form in any medium by electronic means that enables them to be stored in permanent form and be retrieved and read` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is written material` `it represents or reproduces words, figures or symbols` `it is in a visible and tangible form by any means and in any medium` `it is in a visible form in any medium by electronic means that enables them to be stored in permanent form and be retrieved and read` MEANS
        `it represents or reproduces words, figures or symbols`
    AND (    `it is in a visible and tangible form by any means and in any medium`
          OR `it is in a visible form in any medium by electronic means that enables them to be stored in permanent form and be retrieved and read`)

§ `Section 64 -- Power for secondary legislation to incorporate material by reference`

-- The printed items (a) and (b) are members, and so is each organisation or place they name (ruling C).
DECLARE `Kind of material` IS ONE OF
    `a standard, framework, code of practice, recommended practice or requirement of an international organisation or a national organisation`
    `a standard, framework, code of practice, recommended practice or requirement of an international organisation`
    `a standard, framework, code of practice, recommended practice or requirement of a national organisation`
    `a standard, framework, code of practice, recommended practice or requirement prescribed in any country or jurisdiction, or by any group of countries`
    `a standard, framework, code of practice, recommended practice or requirement prescribed in any country`
    `a standard, framework, code of practice, recommended practice or requirement prescribed in any jurisdiction`
    `a standard, framework, code of practice, recommended practice or requirement prescribed by any group of countries`
    `other written material that deals with technical matters`
    `something else`

-- src:433 | This section is sufficient authority for secondary legislation to incorporate 1 or more of the following by reference:
-- src:434 | a standard, framework, code of practice, recommended practice, or requirement of an international organisation or a national organisation:
-- src:435 | a standard, framework, code of practice, recommended practice, or requirement prescribed in any country or jurisdiction, or by any group of countries:
-- src:436 | any other written material that deals with technical matters if it is reasonable to consider that—
-- src:437 | it is impracticable to include the material in the secondary legislation; or
-- src:438 | the material is so large that including it in the secondary legislation will prevent persons to whom the law applies from using or understanding the secondary legislation with reasonable ease.
-- (1) This section is sufficient authority for secondary legislation to incorporate 1 or more of: (a) a standard ... of an international organisation or a national organisation; (b) a standard ... prescribed in any country or
-- jurisdiction, or by any group of countries; (c) any other written material that deals with technical matters if it is reasonable to consider that (i) it is impracticable to include the material in the secondary legislation; or
-- (ii) the material is so large that including it will prevent persons to whom the law applies from using or understanding the secondary legislation with reasonable ease.
-- Ruling B (fork F11): the function asks whether SECTION 64 is sufficient authority, which is the section's own grant: it has a closed list and (c)'s "if", so technical material that is neither impracticable
-- nor too large, and anything that is not on the list, is not given by section 64: JUST FALSE. That is not a finding that no authority exists: subsection (4) preserves every other power (the s 64(4) function below).
-- src:432 | 64 Power for secondary legislation to incorporate material by reference
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 64(1) (src:432) (src:433-438)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of material`
      `it is reasonable to consider it impracticable to include the material in the secondary legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is reasonable to consider the material so large that including it will prevent persons to whom the law applies from using or understanding the secondary legislation with reasonable ease` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`section 64 is sufficient authority for secondary legislation to incorporate material that is` kind `when` `it is reasonable to consider it impracticable to include the material in the secondary legislation` `or` `it is reasonable to consider the material so large that including it will prevent persons to whom the law applies from using or understanding the secondary legislation with reasonable ease` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `a standard, framework, code of practice, recommended practice or requirement of an international organisation or a national organisation` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a standard, framework, code of practice, recommended practice or requirement of an international organisation` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a standard, framework, code of practice, recommended practice or requirement of a national organisation` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a standard, framework, code of practice, recommended practice or requirement prescribed in any country or jurisdiction, or by any group of countries` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a standard, framework, code of practice, recommended practice or requirement prescribed in any country` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a standard, framework, code of practice, recommended practice or requirement prescribed in any jurisdiction` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a standard, framework, code of practice, recommended practice or requirement prescribed by any group of countries` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `other written material that deals with technical matters` THEN
        IF `it is reasonable to consider it impracticable to include the material in the secondary legislation`
           OR `it is reasonable to consider the material so large that including it will prevent persons to whom the law applies from using or understanding the secondary legislation with reasonable ease`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHEN `something else` THEN JUST FALSE

-- (2) Secondary legislation incorporates material by reference if it does 1 or more of: incorporates the material in whole or in part, and with or without modification; incorporates amendments to which section 66 applies.
-- src:439 | For the purposes of this section, secondary legislation incorporates material by reference if the secondary legislation does 1 or more of the following:
-- src:441 | incorporates amendments to which section 66 applies.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 64(2) (src:439-441)
GIVEN `it incorporates the material in whole or in part, and with or without modification` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it incorporates amendments to which section 66 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`secondary legislation incorporates material by reference` `it incorporates the material in whole or in part, and with or without modification` `it incorporates amendments to which section 66 applies` MEANS
    `it incorporates the material in whole or in part, and with or without modification` OR `it incorporates amendments to which section 66 applies`

-- (3) Material incorporated by reference in reliance on this section has legal effect as part of the legislation that incorporates the material.
-- src:442 | Material incorporated by reference in reliance on this section has legal effect as part of the legislation that incorporates the material.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 64(3) (src:442)
GIVEN `it is incorporated by reference in reliance on section 64` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the material has legal effect as part of the legislation that incorporates it` `it is incorporated by reference in reliance on section 64` MEANS
    `it is incorporated by reference in reliance on section 64`

DECLARE `Other source of authority to incorporate` IS ONE OF
    `any other power in legislation to incorporate material by reference`
    `the ability of legislation to refer to or incorporate other legislation`
    `the ability of legislation to refer to other legislation`
    `the ability of legislation to incorporate other legislation`
    `any rule of law`

-- (4) This provision applies in addition to, and does not limit, any other power, the ability to refer to or incorporate other legislation, or any rule of law.
-- src:443 | This provision applies in addition to, and does not limit, any of the following:
-- src:444 | any other power in legislation to incorporate material by reference (for example, sections 29 to 32 of the Standards and Accreditation Act 2015):
-- src:445 | the ability of legislation to refer to or incorporate other legislation:
-- src:446 | any rule of law.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 64(4) (src:443-446)
GIVEN source IS AN `Other source of authority to incorporate`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 64 limits` source MEANS
    CONSIDER source
    WHEN `any other power in legislation to incorporate material by reference` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the ability of legislation to refer to or incorporate other legislation` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the ability of legislation to refer to other legislation` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the ability of legislation to incorporate other legislation` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `any rule of law` THEN FALSE

§ `Section 65 -- Schedule 2 applies if material incorporated by reference`

-- src:447 | 65 Schedule 2 applies if material incorporated by reference
-- src:448 | Schedule 2 applies if material is incorporated by reference in reliance on section 64.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 65 (src:447) (src:448)
GIVEN `material is incorporated by reference in reliance on section 64` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Schedule 2 applies` `material is incorporated by reference in reliance on section 64` MEANS
    `material is incorporated by reference in reliance on section 64`

§ `Section 66 -- Effect of amendments to material incorporated by reference`

DECLARE `Effect of an amendment to incorporated material` IS ONE OF
    `The amendment has no legal effect as part of the secondary legislation`
    `Section 66 does not deny the amendment legal effect: an exception applies`
    `Section 66 does not apply`

DECLARE `Way material is amended` IS ONE OF
    `it is amended or replaced`
    `it is amended`
    `it is replaced`
    `it expires or is revoked`
    `it expires`
    `it is revoked`
    `it otherwise ceases to have effect`
    `it is untouched`

-- src:449 | 66 Effect of amendments to material incorporated by reference
-- src:450 | This section applies if the material incorporated by reference in secondary legislation in reliance on section 64 is amended by the originator of the material after the secondary legislation is made.
-- src:451 | Those amendments have no legal effect as part of the secondary legislation unless—
-- src:452 | they are specifically incorporated by later legislation made in accordance with Schedule 2; or
-- src:453 | amendments to the material are expressly authorised to have that effect by or under another Act.
-- (1) This section applies if the material incorporated by reference in secondary legislation in reliance on section 64 is amended by the originator of the material after the secondary legislation is made.
-- (2) Those amendments have no legal effect as part of the secondary legislation unless (a) they are specifically incorporated by later legislation made in accordance with Schedule 2; or (b) the amendments
-- are expressly authorised to have that effect by or under another Act.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 66(1) and (2) (src:449) (src:450-453)
GIVEN `the material was incorporated by reference in reliance on section 64` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the originator amended the material after the secondary legislation was made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they are specifically incorporated by later legislation made in accordance with Schedule 2` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they are expressly authorised to have that effect by or under another Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Effect of an amendment to incorporated material`
`what effect the amendments to the incorporated material have` `the material was incorporated by reference in reliance on section 64` `the originator amended the material after the secondary legislation was made` `they are specifically incorporated by later legislation made in accordance with Schedule 2` `they are expressly authorised to have that effect by or under another Act` MEANS
    IF `the material was incorporated by reference in reliance on section 64` AND `the originator amended the material after the secondary legislation was made`
    THEN IF `they are specifically incorporated by later legislation made in accordance with Schedule 2` OR `they are expressly authorised to have that effect by or under another Act`
         THEN `Section 66 does not deny the amendment legal effect: an exception applies`
         ELSE `The amendment has no legal effect as part of the secondary legislation`
    ELSE `Section 66 does not apply`

-- (3) For the purposes of this section, material is amended if the material or any part of it is amended or replaced; or expires or is revoked; or otherwise ceases to have effect.
-- src:454 | For the purposes of this section, material is amended if the material or any part of it—
-- src:455 | is amended or replaced; or
-- src:456 | expires or is revoked; or
-- src:457 | otherwise ceases to have effect.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 66(3) (src:454-457)
GIVEN way IS A `Way material is amended`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the material counts as amended for section 66` way MEANS
    CONSIDER way
    WHEN `it is amended or replaced` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `it is amended` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `it is replaced` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `it expires or is revoked` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `it expires` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `it is revoked` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `it otherwise ceases to have effect` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `it is untouched` THEN FALSE
